{
  "slug": "group-anagrams",
  "title": "Group Anagrams",
  "leetcodeUrl": "https://leetcode.com/problems/group-anagrams/",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "patternId": "hashing",
  "order": 3,
  "summary": "You get a list of words, `strs`. Collect the words into groups so that each group holds words that are anagrams of one another: they use the same letters the same number of times, in any order. Return the groups as a list of lists. Every word lands in exactly one group, repeats and empty strings included. Neither the groups nor the words inside a group need to be in any particular order.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "strs = [\"tone\", \"cat\", \"note\", \"act\", \"dog\"]",
      "output": "[[\"tone\", \"note\"], [\"cat\", \"act\"], [\"dog\"]]",
      "explanation": "\"tone\" and \"note\" use the same four letters, and so do \"cat\" and \"act\". \"dog\" matches no other word, so it gets a group of its own."
    },
    {
      "input": "strs = [\"loop\", \"plop\", \"pool\", \"polo\"]",
      "output": "[[\"loop\", \"pool\", \"polo\"], [\"plop\"]]",
      "explanation": "\"plop\" has the letters l, o and p as well, but two p's and one o, so it isn't an anagram of the other three."
    },
    {
      "input": "strs = [\"ba\", \"\", \"ab\", \"\"]",
      "output": "[[\"ba\", \"ab\"], [\"\", \"\"]]",
      "explanation": "The empty string is a word too. The two empty strings hold the same letters, none at all, so they share a group."
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ len(strs) ≤ 10⁴",
    "0 ≤ len(strs[i]) ≤ 100",
    "Each word contains only lowercase English letters"
  ],
  "targets": {"time": "O(n)", "space": "O(n)"},
  "entry": "groupAnagrams",
